/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/15f4bd7f8ecf8f61ce84858e33cdfa468b0de360fac19b0713b6b2dbc4af8d2e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Equality I is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF} & =\\overset{\\to }{AB}+\\overset{\\to }{FA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FB} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA} & =\\overset{\\to }{DE}+(\\overset{\\to }{EA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BE}+\\overset{\\to }{ED})+\\overset{\\to }{DC} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}+\\overset{\\to }{DC} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BC} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{CB}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/e17584d96cb8d83ccb1abfbd16c4117f58639b7cd3462ee50ad3f31e4eabe279.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}=\\overset{\\to }{BD}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{FC}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Equality I is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC} & =\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+(\\overset{\\to }{AE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =(\\overset{\\to }{CD}+\\overset{\\to }{DE})+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CF} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{FC}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/67706db50684aef52269d20065caa21e4301834835e10e1fd3e456646ae2b32e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DF}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} & =(\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB})+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB} & =\\overset{\\to }{FB}+\\overset{\\to }{BD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80d30ae70bc610593c393707c7def26ded7a17f71ed2299889ad51faf2b6b847" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/state.json" "file_sha256" "2382e8b0a828c1d630ffbdcfa7e374d50a97e807e78e8b57721e628c399e4027" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/7431bd3281e4e49f4caaa5b701885fb64c58196b2256af9d8744decd9a0d0793.png)\n\n  \n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overrightarrow{PS}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{b},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{c},$ and $\\overrightarrow{TS}=\\mathbf{d}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TQ}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c},$ and $\\mathbf{d}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-9934.json" "file_sha256" "980d5d85295de79349e3057d120ad549a606bddca39784d13a79ea2c577e648b" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b, \\mathbf c,$ and $\\mathbf d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TQ}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/4902397acd28e2e5f85063ba55c576d3768360225a705f31a66bd460405dd5a6.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TS}} = \\mathbf{d}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}} = -\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/08086f7e09568f908aa4919a1156d52e465216221be8908e72a1fd90ec8843dd.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{TS}+\\overset{\\to }{SQ} \\\\  & =d+(-b) \\\\  & =d-b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-9934.json" "file_sha256" "980d5d85295de79349e3057d120ad549a606bddca39784d13a79ea2c577e648b" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the diagram shown below, where $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{c}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TS}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/04ce04bf7c7f88d6578c74db0d7398a6d299d11bd9f60f4fc4b6e1bfb0129f3b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-4277.json" "file_sha256" "30b59dc93766fdd2a22ab2a54b4bcd67d6b37f48fa86353c4e816e9f4a8b420f" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b,$ or $\\mathbf c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TP}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{PQ}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{QS}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/53940607b5cbf0220008e6e31ec60f2fd7fd2e4f70c5a8e95e7fcfd64064b095.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TP}} = -\\mathbf{b}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{PQ}} = \\mathbf{a}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{QS}} = \\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/810cce10eb330b1767a101d9107a9534c437daa123f13056a486a9fc96dbab89.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TS} & =\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QS} \\\\  & =-b+a+c \\\\  & =a-b+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-4277.json" "file_sha256" "30b59dc93766fdd2a22ab2a54b4bcd67d6b37f48fa86353c4e816e9f4a8b420f" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/2420154d44b786c6aad54212760e9a37ce67dbdce94a7043039f0e824c5ef9bc.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}-\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AC}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{DC}=\\overrightarrow{BA}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-5015.json" "file_sha256" "5e2f3809db124f9f2c6722505298a9e6cb42989f1a852460de9e2d244b297aa8" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Equality I is true. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}.$\n\n- Equality II is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB}-\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CA} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{AC}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nsince $\\overrightarrow{CA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ have opposite directions.\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{DC}\\neq\\overrightarrow{BA}$ since they have opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/example-5015.json" "file_sha256" "5e2f3809db124f9f2c6722505298a9e6cb42989f1a852460de9e2d244b297aa8" "basis" 1478 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-12049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/2f9e6eff196e24ddabca8d778d27e499fc1b856ef7169257a31a7cbaca8b564b.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TP}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RS}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-12049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/e1d5eb2f392332f69fa1507899b30b838a42ebd1c40dacddeca4edcf0f7aa8c2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PT}=-b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/0e8e24968141284550fac7d4e5c63333789f30ade8f7d5dd8b87fae4e012673a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT} \\\\  & =a+(-b) \\\\  & =a-b\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-12049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b93cf8dcd0b70ef34f2cc0ee1c5921322c3b7b6746cad21697082e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-12049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-12049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a+b"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a+d"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a-b"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b+c"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b-c"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-12049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a-b"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-11323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/36aaf58af536428c74cdb8f4c02c2b4f07e414422e8aea378c75d7abcff58cff.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{YX}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{XV}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{VZ}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{YW}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{XW}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-11323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $X$ to $W$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$  \n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{XW}=\\overset{\\to }{XY}+\\overset{\\to }{YW},\n$$\n\nas shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/4758b51fd3dc076059d60e944de0ad8375bb304240365959d4c6cae94f95a535.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{XY}=-a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{YW}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/e942d61c1f51c36dc6cd04f88ff5e37f538920a34c1af5bc780c47691567b668.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{XW} & =\\overset{\\to }{XY}+\\overset{\\to }{YW} \\\\  & =-a+d \\\\  & =d-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-11323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b93cf8dcd0b70ef34f2cc0ee1c5921322c3b7b6746cad21697082e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-11323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-11323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=a+b-c"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=a-b-c"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=c-a"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=d+a"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=d-a"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-11323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=d-a"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-328086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/6709c80eeddea3d31d68d51816a0249758d5a535eb5f2e6983f8e786faf3f227.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{QT}=$ \n {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-328086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/cd8dc0d2e01927c8b2ca116265b257d835a1baae62272b703610f2947d92a8c2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QS}=-b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{ST}=-c.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/8ed8c71e0d45ae0c9cf7d8a7d2889ee3a79471aaeb408ad0f53f487523daac13.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST} \\\\  & =-b+(-c) \\\\  & =-b-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-328086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b93cf8dcd0b70ef34f2cc0ee1c5921322c3b7b6746cad21697082e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-328086" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-328086" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-b-c"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-142977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/b12b053e195f242bdf15499ee38f9b00830cd9d2a51e17a7df15ccf427b9f9c2.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{PT}$ in terms of $a,b,$ and $c.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-142977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $P$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PT}=\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QT},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/f5a772ed6d71bb8654fc4fc1ad6be444c6c12827b5d582cec1af18b3329ecfb9.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/ad3812200ad6af06a69d8f105c8161b7a772512a5c2ad07e12756256663f20a6.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PT} & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QT} \\\\  & =a+b\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-142977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b93cf8dcd0b70ef34f2cc0ee1c5921322c3b7b6746cad21697082e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-142977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "