" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=a+b"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-335529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/6e5d4cef21454855d29639d236ead4c2ad6cfcb66d2b8adaa7df16405f6d250c.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{TR}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{MP}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{MT}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{QR}=$   \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-335529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $R$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QR}=\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/c42a0b8323c282a573244591d900801194f2f5b7382aabe60dedd903b896a029.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QP}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PM}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{MT}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TR}=a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/9876c3c4947aa9d61e687138bfb6fb26040e7c334af8b02914f5857ae1616e98.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QR} & =\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR} \\\\  & =b-c+d+a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-335529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b93cf8dcd0b70ef34f2cc0ee1c5921322c3b7b6746cad21697082e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-335529" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-335529" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a+b-c+d"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-328099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/40fa465ab7fc211d2e4a9bb8640e12d3bb2d694eae834f514c66e53dc11fd96d.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{ST}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TQ}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=d,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TR}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{SP}$ in terms of vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{SP}=$  \n {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/referen