82e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-335530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-335530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a+b-c"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-142999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/c61b5aec221dd257c507fdaa8f2a04f0f29b158a6ea93afd38a310fc1150669d.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{ST}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TP}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-142999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $S$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=\\overset{\\to }{ST}+\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/abd73b231ee79396e64c018ccfaed752efff4bedc053b1d9977761c283a3b994.png)\n\n  \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{ST}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TP}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=-a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/c560ab74e5d87c51adb19c287b1e75aa2ee112170f3e6361e1b5bc65c182dbda.png)\n\n   \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{ST}+\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =b+d-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-142999" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b93cf8dcd0b70ef34f2cc0ee1c5921322c3b7b6746cad21697082e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-142999" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-142999" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=a+b+d"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=a+c+d"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b+c+d"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b+d-a"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b+d-c"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-142999" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b+d-a"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/86aac25c634d29639329ae53209141ce81a3a82a70d42a4c2dfc6d356ee378b8.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DB}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{CD}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB} & =(\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC})+\\overset{\\to }{CB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA})+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =(\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC})+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{DB}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b93cf8dcd0b70ef34f2cc0ee1c5921322c3b7b6746cad21697082e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-69539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/67706db50684aef52269d20065caa21e4301834835e10e1fd3e456646ae2b32e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DF}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} & =(\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB})+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB} & =\\overset{\\to }{FB}+\\overset{\\to }{BD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b93cf8dcd0b70ef34f2cc0ee1c5921322c3b7b6746cad21697082e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-143001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/e17584d96cb8d83ccb1abfbd16c4117f58639b7cd3462ee50ad3f31e4eabe279.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}=\\overset{\\to }{BD}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{FC}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Equality I is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC} & =\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+(\\overset{\\to }{AE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =(\\overset{\\to }{CD}+\\overset{\\to }{DE})+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CF} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{FC}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b93cf8dcd0b70ef34f2cc0ee1c5921322c3b7b6746cad21697082e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-77389" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-118976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/dcd36221e7ad293f0aac1ab99ece80641cb077efd05adc168a552e97d86100c8.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\overset{\\to }{FA}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-118976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Equality I is false. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{AD}\\ne \\overset{\\to }{CB}$ since they have the opposite directions.\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}.$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\overset{\\to }{AF}\\ne \\overset{\\to }{FA}$ since they have the opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-118976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b93cf8dcd0b70ef34f2cc0ee1c5921322c3b7b6746cad21697082e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-118976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-118976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-118976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/15f4bd7f8ecf8f61ce84858e33cdfa468b0de360fac19b0713b6b2dbc4af8d2e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Equality I is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF} & =\\overset{\\to }{AB}+\\overset{\\to }{FA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FB} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA} & =\\overset{\\to }{DE}+(\\overset{\\to }{EA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BE}+\\overset{\\to }{ED})+\\overset{\\to }{DC} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}+\\overset{\\to }{DC} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BC} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{CB}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b93cf8dcd0b70ef34f2cc0ee1c5921322c3b7b6746cad21697082e8151880d0"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "q-143006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ca47f23e1e016c2b14bafc0e99438ff92f1e725caa9c5eaf5494798edfd1ab"} {"question" "e-9934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/7431bd3281e4e49f4caaa5b701885fb64c58196b2256af9d8744decd9a0d0793.png)\n\n  \n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overrightarrow{PS}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{b},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{c},$ and $\\overrightarrow{TS}=\\mathbf{d}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TQ}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c},$ and $\\mathbf{d}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/example-9934.json" "file_sha256" "4b798f4108c0e8e21728e374a532fdf238a67768490f00df9670255b74a55000"} {"question" "e-9934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b, \\mathbf c,$ and $\\mathbf d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TQ}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/4902397acd28e2e5f85063ba55c576d3768360225a705f31a66bd460405dd5a6.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TS}} = \\mathbf{d}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}} = -\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/08086f7e09568f908aa4919a1156d52e465216221be8908e72a1fd90ec8843dd.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{TS}+\\overset{\\to }{SQ} \\\\  & =d+(-b) \\\\  & =d-b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/example-9934.json" "file_sha256" "4b798f4108c0e8e21728e374a532fdf238a67768490f00df9670255b74a55000"} {"question" "e-4277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the diagram shown below, where $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{c}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TS}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/04ce04bf7c7f88d6578c74db0d7398a6d299d11bd9f60f4fc4b6e1bfb0129f3b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/example-4277.json" "file_sha256" "46a09787651c3e9ebad8f04c4d895517c55b61c102c33a00c5b8e61f1087d623"} {"question" "e-4277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b,$ or $\\mathbf c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TP}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{PQ}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{QS}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/53940607b5cbf0220008e6e31ec60f2fd7fd2e4f70c5a8e95e7fcfd64064b095.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TP}} = -\\mathbf{b}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{PQ}} = \\mathbf{a}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{QS}} = \\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/810cce10eb330b1767a101d9107a9534c437daa123f13056a486a9fc96dbab89.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TS} & =\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QS} \\\\  & =-b+a+c \\\\  & =a-b+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/example-4277.json" "file_sha256" "46a09787651c3e9ebad8f04c4d895517c55b61c102c33a00c5b8e61f1087d623"} {"question" "e-5015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/2420154d44b786c6aad54212760e9a37ce67dbdce94a7043039f0e824c5ef9bc.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}-\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AC}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{DC}=\\overrightarrow{BA}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/example-5015.json" "file_sha256" "ebdae55b9469e15cfc63633d091070cdd62eaaa2b15b2b07365dbe43ba6638d6"} {"question" "e-5015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- Equality I is true. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}.$\n\n- Equality II is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB}-\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CA} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{AC}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nsince $\\overrightarrow{CA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ have opposite directions.\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{DC}\\neq\\overrightarrow{BA}$ since they have opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/example-5015.json" "file_sha256" "ebdae55b9469e15cfc63633d091070cdd62eaaa2b15b2b07365dbe43ba6638d6"}] "usage" {"e-4277" [] "q-143001" [] "q-77389" [] "q-69539" [] "e-9934" [] "e-5015" [] "q-328086" [] "q-143006" []} "basis" 2709 "retractions" [[17592186310363 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/6709c80eeddea3d31d68d51816a0249758d5a535eb5f2e6983f8e786faf3f227.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$ To denote the corresponding vectors, use $a$, $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\n\n$\\overset{\\to }{QT}=$ \n {{field-1}}"] [17592186310363 :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/cd8dc0d2e01927c8b2ca116265b257d835a1baae62272b703610f2947d92a8c2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QS}=-b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{ST}=-c.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/8ed8c71e0d45ae0c9cf7d8a7d2889ee3a79471aaeb408ad0f53f487523daac13.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{ST} \\\\  & =-b+(-c) \\\\  & =-b-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186310377 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/86aac25c634d29639329ae53209141ce81a3a82a70d42a4c2dfc6d356ee378b8.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DB}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BA}-\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{CD}$"] [17592186310336 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/67706db50684aef52269d20065caa21e4301834835e10e1fd3e456646ae2b32e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DF}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}$"] [17592186310384 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/e17584d96cb8d83ccb1abfbd16c4117f58639b7cd3462ee50ad3f31e4eabe279.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}=\\overset{\\to }{BD}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{FC}$"] [17592186310343 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/15f4bd7f8ecf8f61ce84858e33cdfa468b0de360fac19b0713b6b2dbc4af8d2e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$"] [17592186096524 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/7431bd3281e4e49f4caaa5b701885fb64c58196b2256af9d8744decd9a0d0793.png)\n\n  \n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overrightarrow{PS}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{b},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{c},$ and $\\overrightarrow{TS}=\\mathbf{d}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TQ}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c},$ and $\\mathbf{d}.$"] [17592186096524 :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b, \\mathbf c,$ and $\\mathbf d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TQ}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/4902397acd28e2e5f85063ba55c576d3768360225a705f31a66bd460405dd5a6.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TS}} = \\mathbf{d}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}} = -\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/08086f7e09568f908aa4919a1156d52e465216221be8908e72a1fd90ec8843dd.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{TS}+\\overset{\\to }{SQ} \\\\  & =d+(-b) \\\\  & =d-b.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096367 :question/problem "Consider the diagram shown below, where $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{c}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TS}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/04ce04bf7c7f88d6578c74db0d7398a6d299d11bd9f60f4fc4b6e1bfb0129f3b.png)"] [17592186096367 :question/worked-solution "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b,$ or $\\mathbf c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TP}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{PQ}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{QS}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/53940607b5cbf0220008e6e31ec60f2fd7fd2e4f70c5a8e95e7fcfd64064b095.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TP}} = -\\mathbf{b}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{PQ}} = \\mathbf{a}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{QS}} = \\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/810cce10eb330b1767a101d9107a9534c437daa123f13056a486a9fc96dbab89.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TS} & =\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QS} \\\\  & =-b+a+c \\\\  & =a-b+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096409 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/2420154d44b786c6aad54212760e9a37ce67dbdce94a7043039f0e824c5ef9bc.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}-\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AC}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{DC}=\\overrightarrow{BA}$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186310338 17592186310339 17592186310340 17592186310341 17592186310342 17592186310345 17592186310346 17592186310347 17592186310348 17592186310349 17592186310365 17592186310366 17592186310379 17592186310380 17592186310381 17592186310382 17592186310383 17592186310386 17592186310387 17592186310388 17592186310389 17592186310390] "immutable_fields" [[17592186310337 :answer-field/correct] [17592186310337 :answer-field/id] [17592186310337 :answer-field/key] [17592186310337 :answer-field/type] [17592186310344 :answer-field/correct] [17592186310